    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite (a single acceptance test) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`. This repo has just the one test class.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature so `POST /api/owners` accepts an optional `title` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns a composed salutation.\n\nEach piece landed where it belongs, reusing the existing derived-field pattern:\n\n- **`util/SalutationFormatter.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility formatter: `format(title, lastName)` returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/blank. Mirrors the existing `PersonNameFormatter` style.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter (title must round-trip through the DB since the response is read back on a separate GET).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the read-only `salutation` mapping via `SalutationFormatter`. `title` auto-maps (matching property names) on the request-side `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `updateOwner` now keeps `title` in sync, consistent with the other fields it copies.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional input, constrained to `MR|MRS|MS|DR`) to `OwnerFields` and read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` response schema; the DTOs are generated from this at build time.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nThe acceptance test creating an owner with `title=DR`, `lastName=who` reads back `salutation = \"DR who\"`, and the build is green.",
